decision_conditions:
Condition : 17 - The building hereby approved shall have a maximum of 340sqm of non-residential floor area (gross internal) that shall be on the ground floor unless otherwise agreed in writing by the Local Planning Authority, for one or more of the following uses of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987, as amended, or in any provision equivalent to that Class in any statutory instrument revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification:

i) Class A1;
ii) Class A2;
iii) Class A3;
iv) Class D1: except places of worship;
v) Class D2: except nightclubs

In respect of any of the above Class D1 uses hereby approved, notwithstanding the provisions of the Town and Country Planning (Use Classes) Order 1987, as amended, or in any provision equivalent to that Class in any statutory instrument revoking and re-enacting that Order with or without modification; the use shall not be changed to a place of worship without further approval in writing from the Local Planning Authority. Prior to the first commencement of an A3 use, details of a kitchen extract system shall be provided to the Local Planning Authority and approved in writing, and shall be implemented in accordance with approved details.
